# Getting Ready for the Curriculum

This professional learning module gives you a guided preview of the key concepts and instructional approaches used throughout the unit.

Think of this module as a head start: a chance to build familiarity with the ideas your students will encounter, and to start thinking about how you'll teach them in your classroom.

This module highlights important concepts and teaching strategies, but it doesn't replace reviewing individual lesson materials. Take time to review each lesson before teaching it with students.

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## What's in this module?

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: 25px auto;">

  <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 1 - Module Introduction</h3>
    <div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 8px;">You are here</div>
    <div>A short orientation to what this module covers and how to move through it.<br><br><em>5 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

  <div style="background: #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 2 - Web Apps</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #1F1976; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 1-2</div>
    <div>Here's the foundation you'll return to all unit: what makes something a web app, and how users actually interact with one. You'll build a shared vocabulary for the structural components you'll be teaching throughout the unit.<br><br><em>10 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

  <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 3 - Design Foundations</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #555555; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 3-5</div>
    <div>Styling decisions are where accessibility either happens on purpose or gets missed entirely. This lesson covers CSS and how it shapes the user experience of a web app, along with the POUR accessibility principles and how to apply them when styling a page.<br><br><em>20 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

  <div style="background: #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 4 - Interactivity in Web Apps</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #1F1976; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 6-8</div>
    <div>Event listeners and handlers are the mechanism behind every button click and page update your students will build. This lesson introduces JavaScript as the language that makes a web app respond to users, and how the DOM updates a page in real time.<br><br><em>25 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

  <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 5 - JS Functions, Conditionals, and Loops</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #555555; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lessons 9-11</div>
    <div>Reusable functions, if/else conditionals, and loops: these three building blocks show up in nearly everything students write from here on. You'll see how these pieces let students build programs that make decisions and repeat actions.<br><br><em>25 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

  <div style="background: #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3>Lesson 6 - Preparing for the Final Project</h3>
    <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #1F1976; margin-bottom: 6px;">Aligns to curriculum lesson 12</div>
    <div>Guiding students through a final project takes more than good code checks. This lesson focuses on key instructional strategies including collaboration methods, structured feedback, and time management planning.<br><br><em>10 minutes</em></div>
  </div>

</div>

<br>

**Total suggested time:** 90 minutes


---

## Engaging with This Module

As you move through the module, focus on building confidence with the concepts, noticing instructional strategies, and making connections to how students may experience the learning in your classroom.

Throughout these lessons, you'll also see how **AI-supported teaching strategies** connect to each concept along the way.






